251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Five containers hold the base paints \(blue, yellow, white, black, and red\). Each one is connected through IV tubing to its own peristaltic pump, which squeezes the tube with rollers to push out a precise amount of paint. The pumps are driven by L298N motor drivers, controlled by a Raspberry Pi 5. The tubes end over a paint palette with separate wells, and a linear rail actuator moves the outlets along the palette so each mixture lands in its own well. A stepper motor drives the rail through an A4988 driver, and two limit switches mark the ends of its travel. To make a color, the system doses the right amount from each pump into one well, then moves to the next well until all the colors of the artwork are ready.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (The cleaning station is a container with an infrared barrier: a transmitter on one side and a receiver on the other. When the brush is placed in the container, it blocks the beam, and the system detects it. A submersible pump sits in the same container and pushes water through PVC pipes aimed at the brush. The water rinses the paint out and returns to the container, where the pump takes it again, so the same water is recycled. After multiple uses, the water gets dirty with paint, and it can simply be replaced with clean water. When the brush is removed, the beam is restored and the pump stops)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
