>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 187 0 R
/E (Participation in traditional forms of art is declining not only because of a lack of formal education, but also because many people, especially young people, consume art and culture through digital media rather than practicing hands-on techniques. The studies Arts Participation in 2022: A Technical Summary Report, by the National Endowment for the Arts, and New Opportunities for Interest-Driven Arts Learning in a Digital Age, by The Wallace Foundation, show how people participate in artistic activities both in person and through digital media. This highlights the importance of providing opportunities to practice creative activities that require physical interaction with artistic materials.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 187 0 R
/E (Fine motor and sensory skills developed through physical interaction with paintbrushes, textures, and surfaces may receive less practice. The emotional connection to the creative process may also be affected, since the tactile experience of art cannot be fully replicated on screens. Additionally, cultural narratives may become more fragmented as opportunities to learn artistic techniques through practice decrease. Creating an artwork allows people to understand aspects of the process that are not always experienced through digital observation alone.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 187 0 R
/E (Lack of Personalized Feedback in Art Education:)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 187 0 R
/E (The study The Power of Feedback Revisited: A Meta-Analysis of Educational Feedback Research, by Wisniewski, Zierer, and Hattie \(2020\), demonstrates that feedback has a positive influence on learning. Meanwhile, Artificial Intelligence-Supported Art Education \(2022\) examines the use of artificial intelligence to improve art education. The lack of personalized guidance can make it difficult to correct mistakes and develop skills, making specific feedback important for improving artistic learning.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
