<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 188 0 R
/E (The Pixartek project is designed to address the challenges of traditional art education through an innovative solution that revives traditional painting, preserves artistic heritage, and offers a personalized and interactive learning experience, generating a cultural and educational impact. Various recent studies support this approach, demonstrating that artificial intelligence can significantly transform art education through personalized feedback and real-time analysis. For example, a study published in Scientific Reports \(2023\) showed that these systems can analyze artworks and provide recommendations tailored to the user's skill level, improving abilities such as proportion, color, and composition.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 188 0 R
/E (Likewise, more recent studies \(PMC, 2025\) highlight that implementing artificial intelligence in painting courses increases motivation, confidence, and learning retention, while a review published in MDPI \(2024\) concludes that these technologies enhance creativity, active participation, and understanding of cultural contexts. Along the same lines, research published in SAGE Journals \(2025\) demonstrates that real-time feedback allows for continuous monitoring of student progress. However, these studies also point out that most current solutions are limited to digital environments and do not effectively integrate physical artistic practice, leaving a clear opportunity for innovation. In this context, Pixartek emerges as a solution that combines artificial intelligence, computer vision, and technological assistance in a physical system, bridging this gap.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
